  "question": {
    "text": "If $f(x)=\\min \\left\\{1, x^2, x^3\\right\\}$, then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "NiIRx",
      "text": "\n$f(x)$ is continuous everywhere\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SgT8Q",
      "text": "\n$f(x)$ is continuous and differentiable everywhere\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "7xLHN",
      "text": "\n$f(x)$ is not differentiable at two points\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "p2SOy",
      "text": "\n$f(x)$ is not differentiable at one point",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Here, $f(x)=\\min .\\left\\{1, x^2, x^3\\right\\}$ which could be graphically shown as\n$$\n\\therefore \\quad f(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{array}{c}\n1, x \\geq 1 \\\\\nx^3, x < 1\n\\end{array}\\right.\n$$<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/aMjTHolEozuYG-SqnJHOZWv-BUVKNUy9PvmW4-6Za-k.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n$$\n\\Rightarrow f(x) \\text { is continuous for } x \\in R \\text { and not differentiable at } x=1 \\text { due to sharp edge. }\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
